<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- "Play when Idle" (opt-in mod setting, default OFF).

       Targets vanilla's own "Idle colonist" branch of the Humanlike ThinkTreeDef —
       the exact spot a pawn falls into when NOTHING else in the whole think tree gave
       them a job (no food/rest/chemical need, no learning, no work, etc). Vanilla's
       own fallback there is:

         1. If Joy need is below 90%, try JobGiver_IdleJoy (a random joy activity).
         2. Otherwise (or if IdleJoy found nothing), JobGiver_WanderColony.

       Children never have a vanilla Joy need at all (NeedDefOf.Joy declares
       developmentalStageFilter="Adult"), so step 1 always fails for them and they
       ALWAYS fall straight to wandering when idle. This patch inserts our own
       ToddlersPlayExpanded.JobGiver_ChildPlayWhenIdle as a new sibling directly
       before JobGiver_WanderColony — it's a no-op unless the "Play when Idle"
       setting is on, in which case an idle child plays instead of wandering,
       ignoring the play need's normal fullness cap. See JobGiver_ChildPlayWhenIdle.cs
       for the full eligibility rules (still respects TPE_Learning schedule time and
       Work-hour idle suppression, exactly like every other play-vs-schedule check in
       this mod). -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationInsert">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThinkTreeDef[defName="Humanlike"]/thinkRoot/subNodes/li[@Class="ThinkNode_ConditionalColonist"]/subNodes/li[@Class="ThinkNode_Tagger"]/subNodes/li[@Class="JobGiver_WanderColony"]</xpath>
    <order>Prepend</order>
    <value>
      <li Class="ToddlersPlayExpanded.JobGiver_ChildPlayWhenIdle" />
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
